      "writtenOn": "2021-07-12T10:11:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think our current tools let us do any better (or rather, I think it may be the only realistic immediate way for S), but I think this is extremely dangerous. I\u0027m sure we\u0027ll have incidents where someone adds a class but forgets to add it to the jarjar file, with no error, no warning, risking a release that breaks in confusing ways on only some phones, only after we released. We also risk some lib we depend on but don\u0027t control like PlatformProperties adding a class in some other package causing a bug, nobody realizing.\n\nPlease update b/180995093 and show this patch as one more piece of the mounting evidence of how dangerous and error-prone this issue makes the build.",
      "revId": "206257e94ede0388c1d0454c1d8daca2950b4d72",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90cd6413_2c4c0bc1",
        "filename": "service/jarjar-rules.txt",
